      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear the deep self-sacrifice you are trying to give, and it is painful to see your child feel that weight, but please remember that a \"light life\" for your child requires a safe, secure environment that often means you must be present even while struggling. Your child likely feels your effort and hope for them, and that emotional connection is a gift that can help soften the blow of any temporary hardships we all face.\n\nPlease know that you are not alone in this feeling, and reaching out to a mental health professional can help you find healthy ways to process these emotions that might protect both of you. You are doing a hard enough job as it is, and that one life you are living for them is a testament to your love, not a failure.",
